 a  connection form between the two of them  during the second half of the film  well apparently Disney wants one of  these two characters to bond much  earlier than they did in fact Moana and  now we were supposed to become friendly  shortly after sailing off together the  two would have bonded during the song  warrior face in which Maui taught Moana  how to defend herself and seal her bow  at the same time however this musical  number was eventually cut from the  storyline during  interview with cinema blend co-director  John Musker revealed why warrior face  didn't make the final cut according to  him this song felt like it sort of  duplicated some of the other songs and  they wanted a different bonding moment  and the bonding almost came too early  the director added that the song had to  be deleted to prevent Moana and the  demigod from bonding before the  underworld scene could take place all in  all we can't help but agree with Musker  because well Maui's disdain for Moana  and vice-versa was downright hilarious a  very sassy hey hey creating a character  from scratch isn't an easy thing to do  which is why animators tend to draw  inspiration from nature hey hey the  rooster was quickly adopted into the  storyline however his character  development just wasn't resonating with  mallanna's lightheartedness ka was  originally supposed to be a sassy bird  with a very different face in fact the  movies writer Jared Busch revealed that  hey hey started out as a jerk with too  much attitude this pesky rooster was  even made to steal food from puah making  him off as a total bully bush revealed  that he was having a hard time  connecting with the rooster so it was  soon agreed upon to change hey Hays  behavior altogether to make him more  likable Bush gave him a lower IQ and a  string of dopey facial expressions  despite changing the characters core  foundations Bush chose to keep his  original sassy name animators were able  to make the rooster more lovable by  placing him into ridiculous scenarios  it's hard to imagine what Mona's voyage  would have been like without the  dim-witted pet so we're super happy that  Bush chose to put a different spin on  hey haze personality although it's hard  to believe some characters were created  and cut out of the film altogether keep  watching to find out which Moana  personality didn't make it to the finish  line  hooah almost joined Mona's journey  mulana fans were devastated when they  saw the princess Lapua on the shoreline  and sail away many people felt as though  Moana should have brought her porky  friend on board after all who was super  adorable and we would have liked for him  to receive more screen time funny enough  in the earlier drafts  he joined Moana on her quest however it  was later determined that he would stay  behind so why did Disney ditch the pig  and opt for the rooster well because  Moana was supposed to feel out of her  element and  puah helped her feel at home hey hey on  the other hand caused more problems than  he helped solve making him the ideal  companion during an interview with E W  Musker revealed that he still had mixed  feelings about leaving puah behind the  co-director further explained the reason  why he was left out on Mata Nui and this  is what he had to say the pig was  supposed to go with her but we sort of  got talked out of it  they liked mallanna being more isolated  stuck with this idiot rooster and not  having the comfort of having the pig  with her there were cute scenes that we  don't have so there you have it guys the  movie would be completely different if  the pig had been allowed to join on  Mona's epic journey doesn't give you  power to create life it's a homing  beacon of death my team Aoi directors  John Musker and Ron Clements worked  together to create the storyline for the  beloved Disney movie Moana oddly enough  their original draft was nothing like  the movie we know and love when John and  Ron first pitched their idea to  executive producer John Lasseter he was  intrigued but not completely sold  originally John and Ron wanted to create  a movie called mighty Maui and Maui was  set to play the lead character as a  matter of fact Moana wasn't even a  concept yet the directors were intrigued  by ancient Maui myths and wanted to mash  up some of the dummy gods best stories  into one great film  however Lasseter chose to send the  directors to a string of Pacific Islands  so they could get a real grasp of the  culture it didn't take long for John and  Ron to fall in love with the islands and  the way of the people they soon realized  that navigation played a huge role in  this part of the world's history on top  of that they quickly picked up on how  the locals saw the ocean as a living and  breathing bean so by the end of their  trip the directors had a very different  storyline in mind and this is how chief  mallanna's story came to life baby Moana  when Moana was just a baby the ocean  came to pay her a visit  the opening scene showed viewers just  how connected Moana was to the ocean  despite not being allowed to venture  into its depths from the looks of it  Moana was chosen by the ocean a long  time ago heck it even brought her to  defeat his heart for safekeeping  although the sea has a scary reputation  this scene showed us just how gentle and  caring it could be the movies directors  wanted to give the ocean a bold analogy  and this on-screen moment seemed to do  it justice  so it's hard to believe that Disney  almost scrapped this segment while in  search of something better  animators fell in love with Mona's first  encounter with the sea so they were  totally bummed out in the gorgeously  animated sequence was put on the back  burner luckily for us the storyline  later shifted which allowed for it to  slip back in if this scene hadn't made  the cut  fans would have seen Moana become chummy  with the ocean during the first  expedition however we think that their  initial encounter is beyond perfect if  you start singing I'm gonna throw up  bawled Maui Ron Clements and John Musker  knew early on that they wanted to Wayne  Johnson to voice the character Maui so  they felt compelled to model Maui after  his voice actor choosing to make Maui  bald was a very practical decision since  a lot of hard work and money goes into  animated long and bouncy hair however  when the directors pitched their idea to  their advisors they were hit with a  reality check according to the advisers  maui isn't bald he has this long rich  hair that's part of his spiritual energy  so John and Ron told animators to give  Maui a mane of silky hair and they  totally flipped out you see there are  two things animators have trouble  perfecting water and hair and since  Moana is no stranger to oceanic  landscapes and healthy and bouncy hair  animators had their work cut out for  them although mastering Moana and Maui's  Locks was a challenge it helped make the  movie look ultra realistic in fact it's  hard to picture Maui without a single  hair on his head  after all we're so used to his effort  list top knot and luscious curls the a  tide fad you may or may not have noticed  that the Moana movie has a few eight  eyed bats in it this strange animal once  had a huge role in this film  however the 8id bat was eventually cut  from the movies production still it  managed to make a few small appearances  which makes sense considering the  character had already been designed we  clearly see Maui roll the bat into a  ball and send it flying during his song  you're welcome and the battery appears  for a split second when Maui and Moana  first venture into the monster realm so  what's the big deal about this bat and  why does he keep popping up throughout  the film  well the a tied bat was supposed to be a  gigantic monster who tried to stop our  heroes from entering la loti  in fact an entire scene was created with  the bat as the main antagonist in the  scene Maui and Moana were shown blowing  into coconuts to distract the bat with  hopes of getting past him the a died fat  was part of their earliest drafts so  when things began to change his scene  was deleted  grandma Tala almost didn't make the cut  although it may be hard to believe  grandma Tala was one of the last  characters to be added to the Moana  storyline it took writers a few rewrites  before they realized that a wise and  fearless personality could help this  story unfold after all it was grandma  Tala who helped Moana reconnect with her  ancestral roots on top of that grandma  Tala also encouraged Moana to return to  feed his heart to its rightful owner  despite chief TUI's strict orders  without grandma Tala  Milana story would definitely be a mess  without her grandmother's divine  intervention the Polynesian princess  would never have had the courage to keep  on going during their trip to the  Pacific Islands director John and Ron  met a woman named nanano Murphy this  woman was used as inspiration for  Grandma Tallis character so basically if  there's a real-life Grimm out there and  she's super spectacular is something you  want to hear the alternate ending Moana  teaches us a very important lesson at  the end of the film it teaches us that  people can heal and restore their true  beauty even after losing a part of their  heart when Maui stole to feed his heart  he turned her in to take ah a villainous  monster whose grief would eventually  swallow the world finding the perfect  ending for this film proved to be a real  challenge which is why many endings were  created and rejected in fact Moana was  originally going to end with Maui  returning to feed his heart however  producers felt that this made Maui the  star of the third act and they wanted  their girl Moana to be the hero for the  longest time Moana was convinced that  her mission was to bring Maui to tepee  tea but during the final battle she  realized that her mission had been to  return the heart herself all along a  handful of alternate endings nearly made  it to the finish line but in the end  directors fell in love with the one  that's currently being used in earlier  versions motu nui was made to sink to  the bottom of the ocean only to be  pulled back up by Maui's hook  luckily the island was able to remain in  peace during Mona's absence before you  go let us know  which behind-the-scenes secret was your  favorite in the comments below give this  video a big thumbs up if you think hua  is the cutest for more videos like this  one make sure to subscribe to the things  thanks for watching and see you next  time  [Music]

